{"id": "DejwaUJze8y", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Can you carve a whole temple out of ONE rock? 🛕 At Ellora, 1,200 years ago, they did. Kailasa was never built. It was carved.\n\nNo bricks, no blocks, no mortar: just one hill of basalt. The carvers cut three giant trenches straight down into the hill, left an island of rock standing, and carved it from the TOP down: the tower first, then the halls, then the very floor they stood on. Up to 200,000 tonnes of rock came out by hand, and nothing could be added back.\n\nWhat remained: a shrine over 30 m tall on a plinth of stone elephants, Nandi in his own pavilion joined by a bridge of rock, and Ravana lifting Mount Kailash on its wall.\n\nA copper plate from 812 CE says the gods in their sky-chariots were struck with wonder: “This temple made itself.” And its architect asked, “Oh, how was it that I built it?” 🙏\n\nWhich temple should we explain next? Comment its name 👇 Save this for your Ellora trip, and share it with someone who loves temples.\n\nMore temples and stories of Shiva: follow @therishikatha · rishikatha.com (link in bio)\n\n#kailasatemple #ellora #elloracaves #kailashtemple #templearchitecture indianarchitecture ancientindia mahadev shiva harharmahadev rockcut unesco maharashtra incredibleindia rishikatha", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1792161255, "like_count": 172, "comment_count": 8, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1431028618353966a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 61.655, "asr": 44100, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr2-3.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQMEe1Ax7DTmy4_E8g8FZYtzo24ggGU-O5UFLHkOL7VeQN-p7z8KOXt6TyCvvj-bJrzm2D5Z2cq7uuYBvyQCMa0Sgo95q5_tDMn3lgo.mp4?_nc_cat=101&_nc_oc=Adog6FC51em03X4FQAwCMohyvwGnmV68Fwob4fFpgxjhmGmQwh7TeInqWCQcBjeTmYDaV-H6IUcSTfYwO4Ntzuge&_nc_sid=9ca05